  "title": "Upwork’s New $2.99 Withdrawal Fee: Don’t Let It Cost You Twice",
  "summary": "<figure class=\"wp-block-image size-large\"><img loading=\"lazy\" decoding=\"async\" width=\"1024\" height=\"577\" src=\"/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/16023805/Upworks-New-2.99-Withdrawal-Fee-Dont-Let-It-Cost-You-Twice-1024x577.png\" alt=\"Upwork's New $2.99 Withdrawal Fee: Don't Let It Cost You Twice\" class=\"wp-image-1474\" srcset=\"/wp-content/uploads/2026/08/16023805/Upworks-New-2.99-Withdrawal-Fee-Dont-Let-It-Cost-You-Twice-1024x577.png 1024w, /wp-content/uploads/2026/08/16023805/Upworks-New-2.99-Withdrawal-Fee-Dont-Let-It-Cost-You-Twice-300x169.png 300w, /wp-content/uploads/2026/08/16023805/Upworks-New-2.99-Withdrawal-Fee-Dont-Let-It-Cost-You-Twice-768x433.png 768w, /wp-content/uploads/2026/08/16023805/Upworks-New-2.99-Withdrawal-Fee-Dont-Let-It-Cost-You-Twice.png 1280w\" sizes=\"auto, (max-width: 1024px) 100vw, 1024px\" /></figure> <p>Starting September 1, 2026, Upwork will apply a new $2.99 Upwork withdrawal fee to every Direct to U.S. Bank withdrawal made by freelancers whose tax address is outside the United States. The announcement caught many freelancers off guard, since Direct to U.S. Bank has long been the one free withdrawal option on the platform. For Nigerian freelancers, the new fee directly affects a withdrawal method millions have",
